  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1111 AM MST Mon Nov 9 2026\n\nClouds continue to increase ahead of the next incoming storm.\nThe bulk of that low races by to our north tonight and tomorrow.\nThis will bring some light showers, with any real chance of\nmeasurable precipitation across the central mountains. There\ncould be some sprinkles/flurries along the Montana border\ntomorrow, but that potential is VERY LOW at the moment. Any rain\nor snow amounts will be very light, and most likely confined to\naround the Stanley Basin and Frank Church into Lemhi County.\nThere will be some wind gusts around in the 15-30 mph range in\nsome spots. Otherwise, strong high pressure builds until we get\nto the end of the week. Warm spots through Friday will be in the\nlow to mid 60s, which is 5-10 degrees ABOVE AVERAGE. There is a\n20-50% chance of exceeding 65 across portions of the Magic\nValley and lowlands toward Oakley and Malta. We will need to be\nmindful of any inversions that might develop that could temper\nany warmup, or produce some morning clouds or fog. By next\nweekend, the pattern switches to general low pressure west of\nthe Divide. We have a system swinging through Saturday, the\nanother late in the weekend and early next week. The first\nsystem may arrive as early as Friday evening precipitation-wise,\nbut more likely any impact coming on Saturday. High temperatures\nat that point drop back into the 40s and 50s.",
